---
// The shared section header: an eyebrow label, an <h2> and an optional intro paragraph. Ten core
// blocks rendered this same four-line markup, and it had already drifted — five spellings of the
// wrapper class, an `mt-2 text-text-primary` on some headings and not others, and in two blocks a
// missing `(eyebrow || heading) &&` guard that left an empty flex column still eating the header's
// bottom margin. One component makes the guard structural and the drift impossible.
//
// It carries no visual values: everything lives in the `section-header` / `section-eyebrow` /
// `section-heading` / `section-intro` shortcuts, so a site retunes every section header at once by
// redefining those keys — same seam as every other block.
//
// The `action` slot exists because "no props, ever" already backfired: the smbp home needed a
// header with an inline action beside the heading (a link pill), and with nowhere to put it the
// site layer re-implemented the whole eyebrow/heading markup in its own component instead of
// composing this one — the exact drift this extraction removes. An unused slot renders nothing, so
// it costs the other ten call sites literally zero.
// `animation` is here rather than in the one block that first wanted it (#1416): "an illustration
// under the section heading" is a property of the header, and the header is already the one place
// eleven blocks share. Optional, so the call sites that pass nothing render exactly as before.
//
// CORE SHIPS NO PLAYER. It emits the element and the source and stops there — no library, no
// third-party script, nothing on a page that has no animation. That is deliberate and it is the
// second half of #1647: core used to hardcode one client's Lottie files and pull a player from
// unpkg.com on every page carrying a hero, which 404'd on every other client and put a third-party
// request in the shared engine. Which library animates this — and whether one does at all — is the
// site's decision, made where fonts and brand CSS are made. `diligently.pl` already answers it
// well (`src/lib/lottie.ts`: a self-hosted dependency, imported dynamically, skipped below a
// viewport floor so a phone never pays for 375KB), and that answer belongs to that site rather
// than to everyone who installs core.
//
// So the contract is the DOM: a `.section-animation` element carrying `data-animation-src`. A site
// mounts it; a site that does not gets a sized, empty, decorative box and no requests.

import { alignClasses } from '../lib/align'
import HeadingIcon from './HeadingIcon.astro'

interface Props {
  eyebrow?: string
  heading?: string
  intro?: string
  /**
   * The client's own glyph, raw SVG as pasted (the `heading_icon` universal part, dashboard#1968).
   * Drawn ABOVE the eyebrow: this cluster is a centred flex column and the glyph tops it, so it
   * reads as the first line of the header rather than as decoration floating beside one.
   *
   * Passed through untouched — HeadingIcon.astro owns the sanitize-and-theme step, so there is
   * exactly one place that can forget it.
   */
  headingIcon?: string
  /** A JSON animation this site serves (the `$sectionAnimation` field in the block registry). */
  animation?: string
  /**
   * The block's `align` token (`$sectionAlign` — `left` / `center`; `default` and absent leave
   * the header exactly as this component draws it, class attribute included). Every block that
   * declares the field forwards it here rather than aligning itself: the header IS the cluster
   * the field is about, and it already lives in one place (#1643).
   *
   * `align-text` goes on the outer box — text-align inherits down to the eyebrow, heading and
   * intro — and `align-column` on BOTH boxes, because each is a flex column whose `items-center`
   * would otherwise shrink-wrap its children back to the middle whatever text-align says. See
   * lib/align.ts and the `align-*` shortcuts in core/uno.core.ts.
   */
  align?: string
}

const { eyebrow, heading, intro, animation, align, headingIcon } = Astro.props
const hasAction = Astro.slots.has('action')
---

{
  (eyebrow || heading || intro || animation || hasAction || headingIcon) && (
    <div
      class:list={[
        'section-header',
        hasAction && 'section-header-with-action',
        ...alignClasses(align, 'align-text', 'align-column'),
      ]}
    >
      <div class:list={['section-header-text', ...alignClasses(align, 'align-column')]}>
        <HeadingIcon svg={headingIcon} />
        {eyebrow && <p class="section-eyebrow">{eyebrow}</p>}
        {heading && <h2 class="section-heading">{heading}</h2>}
        {intro && <p class="section-intro">{intro}</p>}
        {animation && <div class="section-animation" data-animation-src={animation} aria-hidden="true" />}
      </div>
      {hasAction && <slot name="action" />}
    </div>
  )
}
